# uno/test/golden/state-transitions-v1.hex
#
# Consensus-binding golden fixtures for the §4.3 verify + apply pipeline
# (§12 P.3 of doc/uno-workchain.md).
#
# Each record pins one (UnoShardState X, Transfer Y) → (UnoShardState X', verdict)
# tuple. The consumer test (uno/test/test-state-transition-golden.cpp) parses
# this file and asserts byte-equality against the running implementation.
#
# Format:
#   record_id=<int, monotonically increasing from 1>
#   label=<short-human-label>
#   verdict=<Ok | one of VerifyResult::* names from uno/core/compute-phase.h>
#   pre_state=<hex byte blob; canonical UnoShardState serialisation>
#   transfer=<hex byte blob; canonical §4.1 wire format>
#   post_state=<hex byte blob; present ONLY when verdict == Ok>
#   ---
#
# Empty hex values are written as empty strings on the right of the `=`.
#
# --- CURRENT STATE (K-fixtures partial population) --------------------------
# Reject records (4-10) carry real Transfer wire bytes produced by
# uno/test/generate-state-transitions-v1.cpp. The pre_state / post_state
# blobs stay empty pending full UnoShardState serializer integration.
#
# Valid records (1-3) remain empty until the M-P2 Plonky3 prover is wired
# into the fixture generator (set UNO_RUN_PROVE_FIXTURES=1 once the prover
# lands and re-run the generator).
#
# --- Records ----------------------------------------------------------------

